  "body": "@mikewest used the \"::\" notation in some material he contributed to the [webuathn spec](https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/), but in webidl, \"::\" is used in comments but is not formally a part of webidl ?  \r\n\r\nAFAICT, the webidl \"::\" notation was for [scopedName](https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/WD-WebIDL-20110712/#prod-ScopedName) which disappeared in the webidl WD following the [webidl Working Draft 12 July 2011](https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/WD-WebIDL-20110712/).",
